* {{audio|blockhead US.ogg|Audio (U.S.A.)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|colloquial}} A [[stupid]] person.
#* {{quote-book
|lang=en
|year=1764
|author=Horace Walpole
|title=The Castle of Otranto
|passage=So I think, '''blockheads''', said Manfred: what is it has scared you thus?}}
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|year=1953|author=Charles Schulz|title=Peanuts|passage="What a '''blockhead''' that Charlie Brown is!"}}
#* {{quote-book
|lang=en
|year=2008
|author={{w|Philip Roth}}
|title={{w|Indignation (novel)|Indignation}}
|section=
|passage= Not all of them, by no means anywhere close to all of them, just the most notable '''blockheads''' among them — three altogether, two freshmen and one sophomore, all of whom were among the first to be expelled the next day — masturbated into pairs of stolen panties...}}
# A [[sideshow]] performer who [[hammer]]s [[nail]]s or similar items through his or her [[nostril]] into the [[nasal cavity]]; [[human blockhead]].
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|year=2005 |title=Stuffed |author=Brian M. Wiprud   |page=262 |ISBN=0440335450 |passage=Waldo was sent that from an elderly '''blockhead''' named Fuzzy in Gibtown, Florida. That's the town to which most freaks retire. }}
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|year=2014|title=A Coney Island Reader: Through Dizzy Gates of Illusion  |author=Louis J. Parascandola & ‎John Parascandola -    |page=306 |ISBN=0231538197 |passage=He is a classic sideshow performer, entertaining crowds with feats such as sword swallowing, fire-eating, and chainsaw juggling. His specialty, however, is the human '''blockhead''' act, hammering six-inch nails up his nostrils. }}
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|year=2016 |title=Staging Stigma: A Critical Examination of the American Freak Show |author=M. Chemers   |page= |ISBN=023061681X |passage=Burkhardt was a legendary figure in the sideshow world, a mentor and instructor to a new generation of '''blockheads''' and other working acts who now train in private classes at Coney Island USA's Sideshow School with Burkhardt's disciple Todd Robbins (Zigun 2006). }}

